 "_about": "RECORDED AGAIN 2026-10-25 (rd/rsvp-seats-first: the owner’s approved RSVP seats-first prototype, “all as recommended” — after “Joyfully accepts” the card says the seats first (“We reserved N seats for you”, tiles You · +1 · +2, one line + ⓘ), then the You step (the name read-only with “Wrong name? Tell the couple”, then “What should we call you?” and Mobile — the contact boxes moved up from the end), then the +1 names (its line now names the seats, the count line and the summary line gone), then the tagging question, then the rest; a No keeps its contact step after the note, posted as `declined_contact_*`; meant for every guest). Before that RECORDED AGAIN 2026-10-24 (rd/held-pass-reply-identity: the card’s default question reads “Will you join us?” — the Event Hub Reply card’s own words, “event” never “celebration” — in place of “Will you celebrate with us?”; a couple’s own question is unchanged; meant for every guest whose couple typed none). Before that RECORDED AGAIN 2026-10-21 (rd/every-hub-button-works: the guest-to-host line under the card is a 44 px press, `min-h-[40px]` → `min-h-[44px]` in guest-to-host-cta.tsx — the Hub button walk; only the three “a host pitch” cases move, same byte length; meant for every guest). Before that RECORDED AGAIN 2026-10-13 (rd/hub-leftovers item 2 again, batch-4 walk: the terms line is a wrapping flex row whose links are 44px boxes of their own — no two press zones overlap when “Privacy Notice” wraps; meant for every guest). Before that RECORDED AGAIN 2026-10-13 (rd/hub-leftovers item 2: the terms line’s two links are positioned above the sentence text and “Privacy Notice” does not break — meant for every guest). Before that RECORDED AGAIN 2026-10-13 (rd/hub-leftovers item 1: every later step’s question — tagging, plus-ones, meal, dietary, song, note, contact — wears step 1’s 32 px question line, one-at-a-time cards only; meant for every guest). Before that RECORDED AGAIN 2026-10-13 (release batch 3 joining main: #